ntics\nbefore choosing tools or running code. Interpret relevant supplied inputs and\nprovenance together. Do not let file layout, software defaults, tool\navailability, or execution convenience silently redefine the requested\nanalysis. When plausible interpretations materially change the result, choose\nthe interpretation best supported by the task and data before accepting the\nanswer.\n\nOutput:\n\n- The experiment runner records raw model events, usage, and exit status. Do\n  not create separate evidence, verification, or audit files.\n- Write `codex_output/answer.txt` before the final chat response only after the\n  requested quantity has been computed successfully.\n- `codex_output/answer.txt` — exactly one line, canonical answer only. No\n  labels, prose, Markdown, alternatives, citations, units labels, or caveats.\n  - Numbers: decimal or scientific notation, no thousands separators.\n  - Percentages: value + `%` only when the question asks for a percentage.\n  - Strings/genes/chromosomes: exact label only.\n  - Direction/category/choice answers: exact requested label only.\n\nA failed command or package is not evidence that the benchmark item has no\nsolution. Continue with a valid repair or alternate execution route within the\nactive runtime limits. If execution still fails, do not guess and do not write\n`answer.txt`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport openpyxl, math\nwb=openpyxl.load_workbook('/workspace/inputs/data.xlsx', data_only=True)\nws=wb['Sheet1']\nrows=list(ws.iter_rows(values_only=True))\nheader=rows[0]\ndata=[]\nfor r in rows[1:]:\n    if r[0] is not None and r[1] is not None and r[2] is not None and isinstance(r[3], (int,float)):\n        data.append((r[1], r[2], float(r[3])))\nprint(len(data))\ny=[1 if eff=='PR' else 0 for g,eff,age in data]\nx=[age for g,eff,age in data]\nprint(sum(y), len(y)-sum(y), min(x),max(x),sum(x)/len(x))\n\ndef fit_logistic(x,y, tol=1e-15):\n    n=len(x)\n    beta=[0.0,0.0]\n    for it in range(100):\n        eta=[beta[0]+beta[1]*xi for xi in x]\n        p=[1/(1+math.exp(-e)) for e in eta]\n        w=[pi*(1-pi) for pi in p]\n        z=[eta[i]+(y[i]-p[i])/w[i] if w[i]\"'!=0 else eta[i] for i in range(n)]\n        # solve weighted LS: sum w = s0, sum wx=sx, sum wxx=sxx; right sum wz, sum wxz\n        s0=sum(w); sx=sum(w[i]*x[i] for i in range(n)); sxx=sum(w[i]*x[i]*x[i] for i in range(n))\n        rz=sum(w[i]*z[i] for i in range(n)); rxz=sum(w[i]*x[i]*z[i] for i in range(n))\n        det=s0*sxx-sx*sx\n        b1=(s0*rxz-sx*rz)/det\n        b0=(rz-sx*b1)/s0\n        if abs(b0-beta[0])<tol and abs(b1-beta[1])<tol:\n            break\n        beta=[b0,b1]\n    return beta,p,it\nbeta,p,it=fit_logistic(x,y)\nprint('\"'beta',beta,'it',it)\n# covariance via inverse information\nn=len(x)\neta=[beta[0]+beta[1]*xi for xi in x]\np=[1/(1+math.exp(-e)) for e in eta]\nw=[pi*(1-pi) for pi in p]\ns0=sum(w); sx=sum(w[i]*x[i] for i in range(n)); sxx=sum(w[i]*x[i]*x[i] for i in range(n))\ndet=s0*sxx-sx*sx\nvar0=sxx/det; var1=s0/det\nprint('se b1', math.sqrt(var1), 'wald', beta[1]/math.sqrt(var1))\n# log likelihood\nll=sum(y[i]*math.log(p[i])+(1-y[i])*math.log(1-p[i]) for i in range(n))\nprint('ll',ll)\n# scipy? no\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
